__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
.env.local
!.env.example
# Fetched asset mirror: ~1.1 GB of USDs, textures and MDLs downloaded by
# assets/fetch_assets.sh, which reproduces it exactly from asset_list.tsv.
# fetch_assets.sh mirrors bucket keys verbatim, so EVERYTHING lands under
# assets/Assets/ — ignoring the whole directory is what actually keeps binaries
# out (the earlier *.usd*/textures/ patterns missed .png/.jpg under
# assets/Assets/**/Textures/ and staged 1.1 GB).
# Tracked instead: asset_list.tsv, checksums.txt, manifest.json (AGENTS.md rule 7).
assets/Assets/
# scratch
*.tmp
_staging/
# kit run logs (large, regenerated); curated evidence lives in the task entry.
# `results/logs/*` rather than `results/logs/`: git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, and the README below must be tracked.
results/logs/*
# …except the log POLICY + benign-noise allowlist + batch canary checklist,
# which is curated evidence the T4.3 canary greps against (gaps G13/G22/G23).
!results/logs/README.md
# Intermediate per-frame PNG dumps from the recorder / camera smoke tests.
# The mp4s and filmstrips they produce ARE committed; the raw frames are bulky
# and fully regenerable.
results/**/*_frames/

# T2.4 camera-offset sweep output: 27 MB of regenerable debug frames.
# The script (scripts/debug_viewer_offset.py) is tracked; its output is not.
results/figures/smoke/viewer_offsets/
